From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: register child before allowing execution

Some tests intentionally terminate a child immediately after it starts.  The
SIGCHLD handler can therefore reap the child before start_child records it,
after which start_child overwrites the completed state with running = 1 and
wait_for_type waits forever.

Use a pipe as a one-byte start barrier.  The child cannot execute its callback
until the parent has recorded the PID, while all test callbacks and assertions
remain unchanged.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: BSD-2-Clause
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 tests/TestUtils.pm | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/tests/TestUtils.pm
+++ b/tests/TestUtils.pm
@@ -34,0 +35,3 @@
+    pipe(my $ready_read, my $ready_write)
+        or die("pipe: $!");
+
@@ -36,0 +40,2 @@
+        close($ready_read);
+        close($ready_write);
@@ -38,0 +44,6 @@
+        close($ready_write);
+        my $ready = '';
+        my $bytes = sysread($ready_read, $ready, 1);
+        die("parent did not release child: $!")
+            unless defined($bytes) && $bytes == 1;
+        close($ready_read);
@@ -44,0 +56 @@
+    close($ready_read);
@@ -53,0 +66,5 @@
+    my $bytes = syswrite($ready_write, '1', 1);
+    close($ready_write);
+    die("failed to release child: $!")
+        unless defined($bytes) && $bytes == 1;
+
--
